      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "from-pretrained-refuses-where-it-used-to-warn",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "from_pretrained now returns Err when any adapter tensor fits no q_proj/v_proj slot (line 95, the new ?). A third-party PEFT adapter trained with more target modules (k_proj, o_proj, MLP; all-linear is a common PEFT default) now aborts the whole pipeline load, where at the base it loaded with V slots overwritten. That refusal is what the contract asks for. But the Err arm of load_adapter_peft one branch down still prints a warning and continues with the base model, so an unreadable adapter loads and an unplaceable one does not. The two failure modes of one adapter file now behave in opposite ways, and neither the PR text nor the contract says which is intended."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "crates/aprender-train/src/finetune/instruct_pipeline/constructors.rs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 95
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "git",
              "grep",
              "-n",
              "-e",
              "failed to load: {e}",
              "--",
              "crates/aprender-train/src/finetune/instruct_pipeline/constructors.rs"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "678a7bc185975b43f7bf45fb8d03e2f6a32d8d08fd77a552e788900c0ed569a7",
            "failure_scenario": "examples/ssc_eval.rs (expect on from_pretrained) panics on a model dir holding an all-linear PEFT adapter, while the same dir with a truncated adapter file loads the base model silently and reports scores for it.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "lora-rank-zero-with-adapter-now-refuses",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "With lora_rank 0, build_lora_layers returns no slots, so slot_len is None for every tensor and any adapter_model.safetensors in the model dir makes from_pretrained fail. At the base the loop skipped every tensor and the base model loaded. No in-tree path reaches this today: the lora_rank 0 configs are InstructPipeline::new in a test and the wgpu trainer, neither of which calls from_pretrained. Latent, so a note."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "crates/aprender-train/src/finetune/instruct_pipeline/constructors.rs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 360
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "git",
              "grep",
              "-n",
              "-e",
              "lora_rank: 0",
              "--",
              "crates/aprender-train",
              "crates/apr-cli"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "1b6ac98de222137b6035ec2406b314b5a0815558b460cd4f3c07db8719989da5",
            "failure_scenario": "A future base-model eval that sets lora_rank 0 on a fine-tuned model dir fails with an adapter error instead of evaluating the base.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "error-propagation-untested-at-from-pretrained",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The three new tests call inject_adapter_weights directly. No test in instruct_pipeline writes an adapter_model.safetensors and calls from_pretrained: the only matches for adapter_model there are the two lines of from_pretrained itself. So replacing the new ? on line 95 with .ok() or let _ = compiles and passes every test, and the refusal the contract describes stops reaching the caller."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "crates/aprender-train/src/finetune/instruct_pipeline/constructors.rs"
                },
                "region": {
