            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "failure_scenario": "If the test didn't assert that 'snapshot(&layers) == before', a defect that failed to completely revert or prevent partial layer writes would incorrectly pass.",
            "rationale": "agy judgement. agy marked this measured, but returned no excerpt digest or exit code, so the primary records it as asserted; reverified_by_primary is false."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "agy-behavior-change-from-pretrained",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The new error path propagated by the '?' operator in 'from_pretrained' alters the behavior for callers. Specifically, adapters with extra target modules (like 'k_proj' or 'mlp') will now hard-fail instead of silently overwriting 'v_proj'. Additionally, if 'lora_rank=0', the empty 'lora_layers' means any existing adapter tensors are unplaceable, causing a refusal error where it previously skipped them silently."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "crates/aprender-train/src/finetune/instruct_pipeline/constructors.rs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "failure_scenario": "A caller requesting 'lora_rank=0' in a directory that happens to contain an adapter file will now encounter a fatal error instead of gracefully loading the base model, because the adapter tensors cannot be placed in the zero-length 'lora_layers' array.",
            "rationale": "agy judgement. agy marked this asserted, but returned no excerpt digest or exit code, so the primary records it as asserted; reverified_by_primary is false."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "agy-contract-matches-code",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The updated contract text perfectly captures the new logic, declaring the formula 'with slot(t) = 2·layer(t) + [proj(t) = v_proj]; otherwise load → Err and ∀ slot: unchanged'. This is mathematically identical to the implemented validation and error-handling steps."
          },
